    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b0",
      "text": "CLIP-Guided SAM\n5\n",
      "bbox": [
        369.68,
        92.72,
        480.6,
        101.69
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1478,
        370,
        1922,
        406
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 8.97,
      "font_name": "SFRM0900",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 17,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b1",
      "text": "CLIPSurgery [22] improves CLIP\u2019s spatial localization by modifying its infer-\nence pathway to produce sharper similarity maps, which can be used to sample\nspatial prompts for SAM, and is a training-free method.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        118.02,
        480.62,
        151.9
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        472,
        1922,
        607
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 210,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b2",
      "text": "Unlike methods that treat CLIP either as the primary segmentation engine\nor solely as an external prompt generator, we use CLIP as a provider of seman-\ntic priors, whose features are injected directly into SAM\u2019s encoder and jointly\noptimized with SAM.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        153.97,
        480.59,
        199.8
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        615,
        1922,
        799
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 251,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b3",
      "text": "2.3\nIntegration of SAM and CLIP for Text-to-Mask Segmentation\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        220.13,
        473.64,
        230.1
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        880,
        1894,
        920
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFBX1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 61,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b4",
      "text": "Existing VLM+SAM systems generally follow two strategies. The first relies on\ncascaded pipelines where a VLM converts text prompts into spatial prompts for\nSAM. Examples include GroundedSAM [29], which uses GroundingDINO [25]\nto generate box prompts, and CLIP-based methods that derive points or masks\nfrom similarity maps [16,17,21,22]. Other approaches use SAM to propose masks,\nwhich are then filtered or scored using CLIP [1,38]. In most cases, SAM and the\nVLM operate as separate stages.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        240.47,
        480.61,
        322.17
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        961,
        1922,
        1288
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 492,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b5",
      "text": "A smaller body of work explores tighter feature-level coupling between SAM\nand VLMs by injecting language signals directly into SAM\u2019s internal represen-\ntations [24, 27, 33, 39, 41]. These approaches typically fuse text embeddings or\nactivation maps through additional tokens, modified decoders, or auxiliary mod-\nules, often departing from the original SAM architecture or requiring substantial\nsupervision and training, and are sometimes tailored to specific domains.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        324.24,
        480.6,
        393.98
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        1296,
        1922,
        1575
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 469,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b6",
      "text": "Our approach bridges these directions. We build on CLIPSurgery-style prompt\nstrategy while also injecting CLIP-derived semantic features directly into SAM\u2019s\nencoder via adapters, enabling internal semantic conditioning and joint SAM and\nCLIP co-adaptation with minimal architectural changes.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        396.06,
        483.75,
        441.88
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        1584,
        1935,
        1767
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 291,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b7",
      "text": "3\nMethod\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        462.66,
        201.08,
        474.61
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        1850,
        804,
        1898
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.96,
      "font_name": "SFBX1200",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 8,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b8",
      "text": "We propose CLIP-Guided SAM, which uses CLIP to produce (i) spatial se-\nmantic prompts and (ii) feature-level conditioning prompts that are injected into\nSAM\u2019s image encoder via semantic adapters. We support two usage modes de-\npending on whether point prompts come from CLIP (text-only inference) or\nfrom user/GT clicks (interactive setting).\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        488.53,
        480.66,
        546.32
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        1954,
        1922,
        2185
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFRM1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 342,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b9",
      "text": "3.1\nGenerating Semantic Prompts with CLIP\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        566.65,
        370.29,
        576.62
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        2266,
        1481,
        2306
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "SFBX1000",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 41,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p5_b10",
      "text": "Given an image and a class prompt, CLIP produces: (i) patch-level image em-\nbeddings V \u2208RN\u00d7Cc (after discarding the [CLS] token, where N = HW), and\n(ii) a global text embedding t \u2208RCc.\n",
      "bbox": [
        134.77,
        586.99,
        480.59,
        620.86
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        539,
        2347,
        1922,
